# The openforge-catalog commit the corpus tests measure against.
#
# Pinned rather than tracking the default branch, because several suites assert
# exact per-family counts (src/materials) and exact facet totals
# (pipeline/catalog.test.ts). An upstream scan that adds tiles would turn those
# into a surprise red build on an unrelated PR. Pinned, an upstream change
# becomes a deliberate update here instead.
#
# One defect in the pinned data is recorded rather than repaired, and a refresh
# will land on it. Two of the four internal-corner blueprint templates carry
# `shape|corner` rather than `shape|internal_corner`; `pipeline/templates.ts`
# censuses them from each fixture's own parts, and `npm run import:catalog`
# fails when that census is anything but the two recorded — including when it
# empties, which is what upstream fixing the tags looks like. The failure names
# what to do next.
#
# To refresh:
#   1. bump OPENFORGE_CATALOG_SHA to the new commit
#   2. mise run facts                     — re-derive the numbers
#   3. npm run import:catalog && npm test  — update any exact assertion that moved
#   4. update docs/architecture-plan.md §2 if a quoted figure changed
#   5. if step 3 fails on the tag census, follow its message: record the new
#      defect or delete the workaround, and update docs/templates-plan.md §9.1
OPENFORGE_CATALOG_REPO=MasterworkTools/openforge-catalog
OPENFORGE_CATALOG_SHA=428289679a0c62ade992a51ef949f47cdc2b9aed
OPENFORGE_FIXTURES_PATH=openforge/db/fixtures/blueprints
